From f56083de588ac979b7a7e0aa14d4ea0a95672f6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:57:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] i2c: standalone i915 GMBUS driver for the KNC SMC

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6: the i915 GMBUS engine in the KNC DBOX is the
I2C master for the system management controller (temperatures, power
rails, fan, ECC state, card serial) read by the micras RAS module.
intel_i2c.c/.h are built on their own under CONFIG_I2C_I915_GMBUS
(no DRM), exporting gmbus_i2c_read/write/write_atomic.

Adaptations for 6.18: a platform_driver over ioremap(DBOX_BASE) with
a local minimal struct intel_gmbus and wait_for/wait_for_atomic
(the i915 headers are long incompatible), only the GMBUS hardware
engine (no bitbang/GPIO half); the i915 Makefile builds just
intel_i2c.o; I2C_CLASS_DDC is gone (6.8).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
